WEBVTT

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:20.680
Oh no, I overslept!

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.160
Oh, that's right...

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:32.150
Newspaper Holiday

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:34.950
Grandma, today is a newspaper holiday,
so I don't have to work.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.050
The town is also very quiet because
of the Obon vacation.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:43.330
It kind of feels good.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:53.740
[Note: Obon is a Japanese spiritual
celebration of the dead.]

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:53.740
Oh, it is Obon...

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:30.830
My First Welcome

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:36.490
Good morning, Kana-chan!

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:41.270
I'm sorry for being so late. I'm going
to make breakfast right away.

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:42.680
All right.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:48.630
Haruka-san, you can't drink alcohol
without any snacks!

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:50.230
If you do that, you'll ruin your stomach!

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:53.620
Oh, but I do have a tasty snack...

00:02:53.620 --> 00:03:00.550
Barrier, barrier, barrier, barrier...

00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:00.550
No no, it's not you, Kana-chan.

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:01.080
What?!

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:05.930
Today's perfect snack is this:

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:10.040
50 km on the Kan-Etsu Expressway
near the Hanazono interchange,

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:13.950
45 km of congestion on the Chuo Expressway,
around the Sagamiko interchange.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:16.370
It looks like this situation will continue
until tomorrow morning,

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:19.200
promising a rough start to the holidays.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.600
Ahh, that really makes the
booze go down well.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:25.450
This is your snack?

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:26.690
That's right!

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.470
Inside these rows and rows of cars,

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:31.410
there must be so many girls who

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:38.010
have to go to the bathroom or are whining.

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:40.650
I can't hold it any more!

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:44.340
No! You said you'd buy me candy!

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:47.160
I feel sick...

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.830
Haruka-san, your imagination is crazy.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.710
No idea what that's about.

00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:00.570
Hinata, Yume, and Co. haven't
woken up and come out yet?

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:01.350
No...

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:06.480
They're free to sleep in, but all that's
going to do is make tomorrow harder.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:11.090
Oh, I think Hinata-san is already awake.

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:14.270
I heard her rummaging around in her room.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:28.220
Long time no see my pretties.

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:30.750
How have you been?

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:35.180
Little 100 Yen-chan born in 1965 isn't here!

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:39.580
Ow!

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:42.300
Ahh, my money!

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:46.480
The flower meaning of sunflower
is "false riches".

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:50.420
Or "I only have eyes for you".

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:54.040
I guess she's not cleaning...

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:59.770
Um, should I go wake up Yume-san
and Yuuki-san?

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:02.730
You don't need to put any effort into that.

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:04.760
They'll come down when they get sick of it.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:07.070
Get sick of it?

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.870
Good morning, Yuuki.

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:25.250
Morning.

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:27.050
Do you want to get up?

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:29.290
Or do you want to sleep a bit more?

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:32.000
Just a little more.

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:33.960
Okay.

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:39.820
Stop, that tickles!

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:41.740
Then join in.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:43.980
All right, you asked for it!

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:07.720
What shall we have for lunch today?

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.260
What are you doing?

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:22.850
Err, uh, well...

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:27.570
Obon?

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:30.140
Yes, for my grandmother.

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:35.900
So if it's okay with you, I'd like to
light a welcome fire for her.

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:37.880
I don't mind.

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:39.740
Thank you very much!

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:45.250
Hey, Kana-chan, how do you celebrate
Obon in your family?

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:48.510
Hm, it's pretty normal.

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:51.780
In the morning we burn Ogara
at the house entrance and...

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:55.350
[Okara = soy pulp]

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:55.350
Wait, you burn okara?
At the house entrance?

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:58.310
I don't think that's what she means.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:02.950
Ogara is well, let's see...

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:12.380
These long white stalks, and you burn them
on the ground or in a baking pan...

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:13.310
Huh?

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:15.410
What's this?

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:16.780
A camp fire!

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:27.000
The welcome fire is set, other than that,
we put out spirit food and fruits.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:27.720
It's basic fare, really.

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:30.760
Then let's do all that stuff.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:31.470
Huh?

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.890
Let's do it the way you used to
do it at home, Kana-chan!

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:40.800
That sounds good, I mean it's
good to do things properly.

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:44.230
Please forget about that thing...

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:50.040
You're so right, let's forget
about a lot of things

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:54.690
and work together to make
this Obon really something!

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:55.910
Hinata-san...

00:07:56.350 --> 00:08:02.150
Wait, you're trying to get out
of losing at this card game.

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:04.210
You're so cheap!

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:06.400
Hey, that's slander.

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:10.180
Then pay what you owe me!

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:13.710
All right, I will! Here you go!

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:14.670
Wha...

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:22.120
All right, Yume and Yuuki are on food duty.
Hinata, you're on flower duty, okay?

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:24.090
Roger!

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:28.060
Kana and Haruka, prepare the Obon shrine.

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:31.050
Noooo.

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:31.050
That's only natural.

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:38.860
Veggies, veggies, veggies!

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:43.490
Fiiishhh!

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:06.990
What's up?

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:13.510
I was just wondering if my grandma
will know that I'm here.

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:16.150
Of course she will.

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:16.820
Really?

00:09:17.210 --> 00:09:22.850
I mean, if I was a grandma, I'd always
want to know where my grandchild is,

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:30.460
what's on her mind, what she's doing,
what she's eating, and so on.

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:32.820
I see!

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:37.810
Grandma, I'm here.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:42.630
Yes, and what kind of panties
she's wearing today,

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:47.260
how her breasts are today, or how
her peachy butt is doing...

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:50.180
Oh my, squeeze squeeze!

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:57.200
Chief, what's that?

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:58.820
An Obon gift that someone sent.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:01.460
Let's put it up there while we're at it.

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:04.530
Wow, thank you so much.

00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:06.450
It's just because it's already here.

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:11.660
By the way, do you actually have the
mortuary tablet and a portrait?

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:18.020
Yes. It's not a photograph, but I have
a portrait I made in art class.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:22.340
Uh, can you actually recognize her in it?

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:25.830
That thing was like that because
I drew it hastily!

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:29.010
If I have time I can draw properly!

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:30.490
Are all pickles created equal?

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:45.690
These flowers remind me of
a pachinko arcade opening!

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:50.840
Aren't they good? They're vivid and the best
thing was that they were free! Free!

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:54.090
I don't think that's something
to brag about...

00:10:57.890 --> 00:11:01.850
Shall we light the welcome fire then?

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:27.940
Aren't you going to make
an eggplant horse?

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:32.000
Oh, that's not a horse. It's actually a cow.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:36.870
Huh? So the cucumber is a horse,
but the eggplant is a moo moo?

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:42.620
Obon is a time when the deceased
come back to this world.

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:44.970
So when you welcome them,

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:48.740
you wish for them to "get here quickly",

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:51.320
so you keep a fast horse ready.

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:52.760
Okay.

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:56.390
But on the other hand, when it's
time to say good bye again,

00:11:56.390 --> 00:12:01.040
you wish for them to "leave
slowly", so then it's a cow.

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:06.550
Aha. Haruharu, you're kind
of like a grandmother.

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:16.270
I hope that your grandma will follow
this path to come back here quickly.

00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:17.280
Me too.

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:19.290
I don't know if she needs to come back.

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:24.800
She might have been too worried
about Kana to leave.

00:12:25.150 --> 00:12:30.830
True, I mean she's so clumsy
and she's always air-headed;

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:33.950
I bet her grandma couldn't leave her alone.

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:34.730
But... but...

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:39.430
That's right, grandma Haruharu is also
so worried about my Kana-chan.

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:44.590
So worried...

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:44.580
What exactly are you worried about?

00:12:58.300 --> 00:13:01.520
It looks like the Obon dance has started.

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:05.050
Oh yeah, I guess it is that time.

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:06.780
Hey, did you know?

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:12.010
There are tons of shops here for the
Obon dance, so it's like a festival.

00:13:13.490 --> 00:13:15.750
Like a festival...

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:23.750
Here I go...

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:48.940
What's wrong, Kana?

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:55.940
I think I might have left the stove
on. I'm going to go check.

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:07.590
It looks like the stove was okay.

00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:09.380
Yes.

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:14.140
The festival sounds like fun, huh?

00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:15.190
Yes...

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:17.590
Kana, do you like festivals?

00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:21.550
Yes, I often went with my grandma.

00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:22.650
I see.

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:26.410
Well then, come here for a sec.

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:32.590
Since we actually have a day off,

00:14:32.590 --> 00:14:35.570
we decided to go to the
Obon dance together.

00:14:35.570 --> 00:14:37.010
Pick any one you like.

00:14:37.010 --> 00:14:38.290
Roger!

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:41.670
Kana, go ahead and pick one too.

00:14:41.670 --> 00:14:45.470
But whose are these?

00:14:45.470 --> 00:14:50.210
Our staff changes quite often, so
a lot of stuff just accumulates.

00:14:50.420 --> 00:14:54.300
How about this one? It's very summery
with the sunflowers.

00:14:54.610 --> 00:14:56.460
Let's see...

00:14:56.460 --> 00:14:58.030
Hey Kana-chan.

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:02.640
What about this firework pattern,
or this lily pattern?

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:06.210
Or do. You. Want. Me?

00:15:10.190 --> 00:15:12.680
I like this one.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:15.910
Isn't that one a bit childish?

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:18.310
You think so?

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:01.740
Grandma, I'm off to the festival.

00:16:13.420 --> 00:16:19.090
Yay, candied apples and bananas dipped in chocolate,
and they have cotton candy too!

00:16:19.090 --> 00:16:21.420
All right, each of you get 1000 Yen.

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:22.870
That much?!

00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:30.910
Hm, if I think of this as extra
income, I could just use it.

00:16:30.910 --> 00:16:32.960
Nonono. But...

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:34.970
Wait, already!?

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:36.900
Hina-chan, this is good!

00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:42.840
I-I can't believe it. I mean cotton candy
is basically just a bunch of sugar.

00:16:42.840 --> 00:16:45.490
How can you buy it without hesitation?

00:16:45.490 --> 00:16:48.890
Well, I mean this stuff is sweet!

00:16:48.890 --> 00:16:51.010
That doesn't answer it!

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:54.440
This is why people who can't
get into college are a drag.

00:16:57.220 --> 00:16:58.930
Are they equal or not?

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:09.550
Kana-chan, are you going to
try to scoop up goldfish?

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:13.590
Yes, I'm actually pretty good at this.

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:23.730
Kana-chan, you're amazing!

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:26.900
All right, I'm going again!

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:29.880
I am the goldfish Kinko.

00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:33.790
Today, I came to the pool with my friends.

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:35.880
Oh, what's this?

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:40.200
This sharp hunter's aiming
for me... I'm scared!

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:42.100
Haruka-san, please stop that!

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:45.040
Space Battleship Nyamato

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:45.040
Meanwhile, in a galaxy far, far away...

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:49.420
So, how is it?

00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:51.800
Whoa, it's totally blue.

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:52.800
What about you?

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:55.350
Ah, it's totally red!

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:05.870
I wonder if they mixed and turned purple.

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:07.110
Maybe.

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:15.790
It's getting quite crowded.

00:18:15.790 --> 00:18:16.780
Geez.

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:20.780
If they have that much time, they should
be at home reading the paper.

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:25.290
But Chief, there's no paper today.

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:30.130
Um, can I keep these goldfish at the office?

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:32.500
I guess you can.

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:34.090
Thank you!

00:18:39.650 --> 00:18:41.970
I'm so sorry!

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:43.680
You didn't look where you were going.

00:18:50.090 --> 00:18:54.460
You're right, I have to look where I'm going.

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:57.340
I want Ramune.

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:02.970
Oh, you're right, I need to make it up to you.

00:19:04.730 --> 00:19:06.320
Here you go.

00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:12.230
All right, I'm off now.

00:19:16.890 --> 00:19:19.760
Next I want octopus balls!

00:19:31.180 --> 00:19:32.980
Cute!

00:19:59.230 --> 00:20:04.550
Huh? Where did everybody go?

00:20:06.360 --> 00:20:09.720
Wow, it's a red dragonfly!

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:13.180
I have to get going now.

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:14.930
I see.

00:20:16.890 --> 00:20:18.100
Hey.

00:20:18.100 --> 00:20:20.110
Yes?

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:24.070
You have to carefully look
where you're going.

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:28.680
Right, I got that. Bye!

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:36.850
You have to carefully look
where you're going.

00:20:44.110 --> 00:20:45.190
Huh?

00:20:45.190 --> 00:20:48.000
Huh? That's it? Geez.

00:20:48.380 --> 00:20:51.400
Oh, Chief, Haruka-san!

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:54.130
We look away for one moment
and you disappear.

00:20:54.130 --> 00:20:56.370
What were you doing!?

00:20:56.370 --> 00:20:58.190
What was I...?

00:20:58.190 --> 00:21:02.420
I bumped into a girl I don't
know and then...

00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:05.430
Do you mean her?

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:14.960
Hi, I'm Keromi. My measurements
are 123, 123, 123.

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:19.020
Damn it! Fried noodles, octopus
balls, mini cake...

00:21:19.020 --> 00:21:22.210
they're all just wheat flour!

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:23.730
Enjoy your time.

00:21:42.430 --> 00:21:44.210
Kana!

00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:47.360
Come down, we're about to
start the farewell fire.

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:50.540
All right, coming!

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:44.820
My First Talk About Memories

00:23:30.960 --> 00:23:33.360
Next time, "My First Talk About Memories"

00:23:33.360 --> 00:23:35.130
Read the paper.

00:23:35.130 --> 00:23:36.680
Really, everything costs money.

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:37.990
You learned another life lesson.

00:23:37.990 --> 00:23:40.300
Now I won't get paid for studying though.

00:23:40.300 --> 00:23:41.670
How is that my concern?

00:23:41.670 --> 00:23:43.550
At this rate you're going to fail the
entrance exam a third time.
